# {{projectName}}

Playwright automation framework with JavaScript and Jest.

## Features
- Playwright for modern browser automation
- Jest test runner with parallel execution
- Page Object Model architecture
- Built-in Playwright reporters
- GitHub Actions CI/CD
- Docker support

## Setup
```bash
npm install
npx playwright install
```

## Run Tests
```bash
npm test              # Run all tests
npm run test:headed   # Run with browser UI
npm run test:smoke    # Smoke tests only
npm run report        # View HTML report
```

## Project Structure
```
{{projectName}}/
├── pages/          # Page Objects
├── tests/          # Test cases
├── utils/          # Utilities
├── config/         # Configuration
└── data/           # Test data
```

{{#if (eq testingPattern "bdd")}}
## Run BDD scenarios

Install dependencies with `npm install`, then run `npm test` (or `npm run test:bdd`).
Cucumber executes `features/` with the selected browser library. Results are written
to `reports/cucumber.json` and `reports/cucumber.html`. Use `HEADLESS=false` to show
the browser. Credentials use `TEST_USERNAME` and `TEST_PASSWORD`; update the sample
selectors and assertions in `step-definitions/` for your application.
{{/if}}
